 "target": 45.0,
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "Greta rolled a giant iron coin down Main Street, dog on top.",
   "s": 0.12,
   "e": 3.433
  },
  {
   "text": "You see, Bellport has 300 holes in its streets, and every one needs a lid.",
   "s": 3.633,
   "e": 7.487
  },
  {
   "text": "Her rival Bruno laughed: \"Round lids? What is this, a pizza shop?\"",
   "s": 7.687,
   "e": 10.934
  },
  {
   "text": "Bruno's square lids were cheaper, so the town bought all three hundred.",
   "s": 11.054,
   "e": 14.235
  },
  {
   "text": "Then came three weeks. Week one: a worker lifted a lid. Clunk. It fell in.",
   "s": 14.435,
   "e": 18.068
  },
  {
   "text": "Week two: twelve lids fell in. But Bruno shrugged: \"Just fish them out!\"",
   "s": 18.268,
   "e": 21.497
  },
  {
   "text": "Week three: trucks bumped the lids, they flipped, and forty dropped in.",
   "s": 21.617,
   "e": 23.928
  },
  {
   "text": "Then Main Street was nothing but holes and traffic cones.",
   "s": 24.328,
   "e": 26.958
  },
  {
   "text": "Ever carried a table through a narrow door? Tilt it, and it slips through.",
   "s": 27.158,
   "e": 30.354
  },
  {
   "text": "A square's diagonal is longer than its side, so a tilted square lid drops in.",
   "s": 30.554,
   "e": 34.582
  },
  {
   "text": "But a circle is the same width every way. Greta's lids can never fall in.",
   "s": 34.782,
   "e": 38.556
  },
  {
   "text": "Bruno begged: \"Greta, can I buy your lids?\"",
   "s": 38.756,
   "e": 40.623
  },
  {
   "text": "She rolled him one. Her dog rode it like a pizza delivery.",
   "s": 40.743,
   "e": 43.73
  }
 ],
